# demo
# `demo/` is deliberately overengineered code MCMR is pointed at on purpose, so the repository's
# own `check .` must not judge it. The kernel's only project-level path exclusion is the Git ignore
# contract, read from the nearest ancestor holding a `.gitignore` and never from above it
# (`src/core/src/discovery/walk/scope.rs`, `parents(false)`). Naming `demo/` here therefore skips
# the subtree for `check .`, while `check demo/` reads `demo/.gitignore` as its own contract root
# and still fires everything. The files are tracked with `git add -f demo`, because Git honors the
# index over this file while the kernel only ever reads the file.
/demo/
